NNAAMMEE
     iiwwii — Intel PRO/Wireless 2200BG/2225BG/2915ABG IEEE 802.11 network driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, include the following lines in
     your kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee iiwwii
           ddeevviiccee iiwwiiffww
           ddeevviiccee ppccii
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann
           ddeevviiccee ffiirrmmwwaarree

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_iwi_load="YES"

     In both cases, place the following line in loader.conf(5) to acknowledge
     the firmware license (see below):

           legal.intel_iwi.license_ack=1

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiwwii driver provides support for Intel PRO/Wireless
     2200BG/2225BG/2915ABG IEEE 802.11a/b/g wireless network devices in
     ssttaattiioonn, aaddhhoocc, and mmoonniittoorr mode operation.  Only one virtual interface
     may be configured at any time.

     This driver requires the firmware built with the iiwwiiffww module to work.
     For the loaded firmware to be enabled for use the license at
     _/_u_s_r_/_s_h_a_r_e_/_d_o_c_/_l_e_g_a_l_/_i_n_t_e_l___i_w_i_._L_I_C_E_N_S_E must be agreed by adding the fol‐
     lowing line to loader.conf(5):

           legal.intel_iwi.license_ack=1

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The iiwwii driver supports the following wireless network devices:

     ••   Intel PRO/Wireless 2200BG MiniPCI Network Connection
     ••   Intel PRO/Wireless 2225BG PCI Network Connection
     ••   Intel PRO/Wireless 2915ABG MiniPCI Network Connection

